# LLDB script to debug the fork crash (issue #210).
#
# Usage:
#   Terminal 1: make debug-qemu
#   Terminal 2: lldb -s tools/debug/fork-crash.lldb
#
# This sets a breakpoint at the crashing instruction (0x4cf55c in busybox)
# and a breakpoint at the page fault handler to catch the crash.

file target/qemu-aarch64/release/kernel
gdb-remote 1234

# Break at the page fault error path in linux-loader
# (the "failed to handle page fault from user mode" error message)
breakpoint set --name handle_page_fault

# Continue - let the kernel boot and wait for shell
continue

# When the shell appears, type 'uname' in the QEMU terminal.
# The breakpoint should hit when the parent crashes after fork.
# At the breakpoint, inspect:
#   reg read x0 x3 x4 x26
#   memory read <address>
